title: The Reprobate Mind – Given Over of God
description: Men given over by God after they reject Him: the three states of man, Romans 1, hardened hearts like Pharaoh's, knowing them by their fruits, past repentance, Sodom, and reprobate nations, from the teachings on the reprobate mind.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-reprobate.html
highlight: reprobate

# One deck for the whole of studies/data/topics/reprobate.json, each theme given the same weight
# (about five slides), instead of a deck per theme. Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed.
# Spelling fixed: "Reparation" -> "Reprobation" (6898), "Kong" -> "King" (10688), "the recruit though" ->
# "they recruit through" (6502), "gambit" -> "gamut" (10013), "least" -> "lest" (5752).
# The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
# from the topic summary and 6898
--- The Reprobate Mind [title]
overline: Doctrine · The reprobate mind
heading: The Reprobate Mind
sub: Men given over by God after they reject Him: Romans 1, hardened hearts, and knowing them by their fruits.
refs: Romans 1:28; Hebrews 6:4-6; Jeremiah 6:30; Titus 1:16
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6898, 10690
--- One of the most overlooked doctrines
big: Romans 1:28 | mark: God gave them over to a reprobate mind
lead: The teaching on reprobation is one of the most overlooked but relevant doctrines in the Bible.
p: It is taught throughout both Old and New Testament, which not only gives description of how one becomes a reprobate, but example after example of those that do, and warning after warning of how to handle them, the evil they do, and the signs to watch for to identify them.

# from 254, 5751
--- Reprobate simply means rejected
lead: Reprobate simply means rejected. Unable to come to saving faith having already rejected God, utterly and finally being given up on by God.
p: Reprobation is a condition caused by belief, and not wishing to retain God in their knowledge, to no longer be bothered by conscience, unwilling to believe and so being given over, given up by God and made unable to. They are given what they want, and made twice-dead.
callout: It is a free will choice as much as salvation, and isn't determined by level or severity of sin.

# from 6898, 279
--- The three states of man
kicker: The three states of man
p: Reprobation, the final and utter rejection by God of those who have finally and utterly rejected His overtures of grace, the call to Christ and the prodding and patience of the Holy Ghost, is one of the three spiritual states of man.
panel: The unregenerate sinner | Dead in spirit but with the conscience of God within, who, until death, could hear the call and believe on Jesus Christ and be saved. They are the children of disobedience.
panel: The saved | Those who call upon the name of the Lord, believing God's testimony and, spirit quickened. They are saved, born again believers. Called the sons of God.
panel-warn: The reprobate | Twice-dead. Conscience seared. Hearts hardened, ears dulled. Unable to come to the knowledge of the truth. Rejected of God. Turned over. Given up. The children of the devil.

# from 279, 5752, 10690
--- Normal unsaved sinners are not reprobates
lead: It's important to recognize that normal unsaved sinners are not reprobates. They haven't been turned over by God.
p: They commit normal sin, common to man, but occasionally have righteous actions and are repulsed by the unnatural lusts of the reprobate, having still a conscience and the law of God written in their hearts.
p: Most people fall in neither the camp of the saints or the reprobate, they are just unregenerate sinners, with all too common lusts of the flesh. There is hope for them until they die, lest they become reprobate.
take: Most people understand perishing, death and Hell. Few people understand salvation and eternal life. Even fewer understand the third spiritual state of man, reprobation.

=== Who are the reprobate
# gathered from 5751, 8591, 11017, 6119, 8143, 5182, 6995: the ways the teachings name
--- Who are the reprobate
kicker: Who are the reprobate
p: It's never about the sin itself, but the state of a man's heart towards God. Yet the Bible names those who have come to it, and the acts that testify to it.
point: Who hold the truth in unrighteousness | and do not like to retain God in their knowledge. [[Romans 1:18]] · [[Romans 1:28]]
point: The Hebrews 6 apostate | once enlightened, who tasted of the heavenly gift, and fell away. [[Hebrews 6:4-6]]
point: The false teacher | reprobate concerning the faith, ever learning and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth. [[2 Timothy 3:7-8]]
--- Who are the reprobate, continued
kicker: Who are the reprobate
point: Who add to or take away from God's word | to knowingly teach a false gospel. [[Revelation 22:18-19]]
point: Who blaspheme the Holy Ghost | which hath never forgiveness. [[Mark 3:28-29]]
point: Who take the mark of the beast | and worship the beast and his image. [[Revelation 14:9-11]]

# from 5751, 10708
--- 1. Who hold the truth in unrighteousness
kicker: Who are the reprobate
big: Romans 1:18 | mark: who hold the truth in unrighteousness
p: Reprobation is a condition caused by belief, and not wishing to retain God in their knowledge, to no longer be bothered by conscience, unwilling to believe and so being given over, given up by God and made unable to.
p: It is rejecting God, His judgment, the conviction of the Spirit, our conscience which is the law of God written in our hearts. The revelation of God's wrath upon sin. They reject all of it.

# from 15201, 15548, 17253
--- 2. The Hebrews 6 apostate
kicker: Who are the reprobate
big: Hebrews 6:4-6 | mark: If they shall fall away, to renew them again unto repentance
p: The bitter end of an apostate, someone who has an understanding intellectually of the things of God, even tasting of the gifts, but in the end rejecting Him. Their destruction is greater than those who simply never sought the truth.
p: They saw the path, maybe followed it for a while, and left it. They tasted of the Spirit, but rejected it without ingesting, without being indwelled. They never fully believe.

# from 11017, 17468
--- 3. The false teacher
kicker: Who are the reprobate
big: 2 Timothy 3:8 | mark: reprobate concerning the faith
p: False teachers are vipers. Reprobates. Dogs. Swine. **Never** able to come to the knowledge of the truth.
p: This isn't someone who is wrong on some secondary or tertiary doctrine. Or someone who disagrees with you about some verse meaning or whatever. It isn't an unsaved person who doesn't understand the Gospel. This is the curse of those who turn the truth of God into a lie. Who knowingly subvert and undermine churches for their own pleasure, recognition or wealth, passing themselves off as men of God.

# from 6119, 6995, 8143
--- 4. Who add to or take away from God's word
kicker: Who are the reprobate
scripture: Revelation 22:18-19 | mark: If any man shall add unto these things; if any man shall take away from the words of the book
p: A penitent believer will be forgiven all manner of sins, but the blasphemy of the Holy Ghost and deliberately changing God's word ([[Revelation 22:18-19|Rev 22]]). These are direct causes of reprobation that most Christians will accept.
p: The same as those who add to or take away from God's word to knowingly teach a false gospel. It's not so much that the sin itself is unpardonable as it is an act that testifies to their reprobate mind. Their hardened heart.

# from 5182, 6119
--- 5. Who blaspheme the Holy Ghost
kicker: Who are the reprobate
scripture: Mark 3:28-30 | mark: he that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost hath never forgiveness
p: The scribes accused Him of being from Satan, and the Holy Ghost by which He cast out these demons, they label an unclean spirit. A blasphemy He warns is unforgivable, and is a way to reprobation and damnation.
p: Jesus teaches that they may slander Him, and be forgiven, but those who falsely accused the Holy Ghost are reprobate. Damned, twice-dead.

# from 8143, 6089
--- 6. Who take the mark
kicker: Who are the reprobate
scripture: Revelation 14:9-11 | mark: If any man worship the beast and his image, and receive his mark
lead: They aren't made reprobate because they took the mark, they take the mark because they are reprobate.
p: The decision to worship the beast and take the mark might be the last straw that leads to God giving them up and giving them over to a reprobate mind, damning them. Just as with all reprobates it's a decision of the heart that does it. It's a free will choice to utterly reject God and salvation.

=== Given over: Romans 1
# from 10676
--- The wrath of God revealed from heaven
kicker: Given over: Romans 1
scripture: Romans 1:18-20 | mark: who hold the truth in unrighteousness; so that they are without excuse
p: Man has a conscience. The law of God is written in our hearts. The Spirit has come to convict men of sin that they may know they need salvation. We see the eternal power of the Godhead and so, all men are without excuse.

# from 10676, 10687
--- When they knew God
kicker: Given over: Romans 1
scripture: Romans 1:21-25 | mark: when they knew God, they glorified him not as God; Wherefore God also gave them up; Who changed the truth of God into a lie
p: So we understand the process, God reveals His truth. Some refuse to see it, and not only refuse (as most people who never believe), but worse, they turn the truth into a lie.

# from 9558, 10707, 10708
--- For this cause God gave them up
kicker: Given over: Romans 1
lead: For... Because that... Wherefore... For this cause... God gave them up... God gave them over to a reprobate mind.
p: Paul describes the cause and effect, conditional phrases that inform the following consequence. It is rejecting God, His judgment, the conviction of the Spirit, our conscience which is the law of God written in our hearts. The revelation of God's wrath upon sin. They reject all of it.
scripture: Romans 1:26-28 | mark: For this cause God gave them up unto vile affections; God gave them over to a reprobate mind

# from 10708
--- Filled with all unrighteousness
kicker: Given over: Romans 1
scripture: Romans 1:29-32 | mark: Being filled with all unrighteousness; Who knowing the judgment of God
p: Many are sins common to man, anyway. We all experience envy, but aren't filled with it. Many commit fornication, many are proud, we boast, we disobey our parents. But we aren't filled with all of it.
p: Especially the implacable and unmerciful trait that they have. They are impossible to please and they seek vengeance and destruction of others, with maliciousness.

# from 5751, 6119, 10707
--- Not the sin, but the heart toward God
kicker: Given over: Romans 1
lead: Reprobate isn't a synonym with depravity or degeneracy. It is the **cause** of such behavior.
p: Unnatural sin is not the cause of reprobation, but a symptom that it's occurred. It is important to get that right. It's never about the sin itself, but the state of a man's heart towards God.
p: This is why you may have a 40yo murderer who, overcome with guilt and coming to the realization of what awaits them, accepts the Gospel sincerely, and you may have a 14yo who has hardly left the house, let alone committed grave sin, who willfully blasphemes the Holy Spirit and rejects God utterly, and is given over to reprobation.
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6898 | The three states of man
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~10687 | Wherefore God gave them up
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~10707 | Cause and effect in Romans 1
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~4025 | Soul winning creates reprobates

=== Hardened hearts
# from 254
--- Pharaoh hardened his own heart
kicker: Hardened hearts
p: In Exodus, we see God through Moses, give Pharaoh multiple chances to acknowledge God and repent, freeing the Hebrews. God sends 10 plagues, and at each we see the pattern:
table: Plague | Pharaoh's heart | Exodus
tr: **Blood** | Pharaoh's heart “became hard” | [[Exodus 7:22]]
tr: **Frogs** | Pharaoh “hardened his own heart” | [[Exodus 8:15]]
tr: **Lice** | Pharaoh's heart “was hard” | [[Exodus 8:19]]
tr: **Flies** | “Pharaoh hardened his own heart” | [[Exodus 8:32]]

--- Pharaoh hardened his own heart, continued
kicker: Hardened hearts
table: Plague | Pharaoh's heart | Exodus
tr: **Livestock die** | Pharaoh's heart “was hard” | [[Exodus 9:7]]
tr: **Boils** | “The {Lord} hardened Pharaoh's heart” | [[Exodus 9:12]]
tr: **Hail** | Pharaoh “hardened his own heart” | [[Exodus 9:34]]
tr: **Locusts** | God announces that he has “hardened Pharaoh's heart” | [[Exodus 10:1]] [[Exodus 10:20]]
tr: **Darkness** | God “hardened Pharaoh's heart” | [[Exodus 10:27]]
tr: **Death of the firstborn** | God “hardened Pharaoh's heart” | [[Exodus 11:10]]

# from 254, 9992
--- Until God hardens it Himself
kicker: Hardened hearts
lead: It isn't until the 6th opportunity that God gives Pharaoh what he has chosen repeatedly, to not acknowledge God when called to.
p: In him we witness the Reprobate Doctrine played out. We see how there are those who, having been given the chance to know God and be healed, refuse. Who prefer a lie to the truth.
callout: They harden their hearts to God's attempts to extend His mercy and grace to them, and in turn God hardens their hearts that they cannot believe.

# from 10013
--- The whole gamut of man
kicker: Hardened hearts
p: As much as the story of Exodus is a picture of salvation in Christ, it covers the entire gamut of human reaction to this gift of grace given us by God.
tile: Believers | who praise God when they hear Moses and Aaron tell them of His promise
tile: Scoffers | in the secular leadership of the people

--- The whole gamut of man, continued
kicker: Hardened hearts
tile: The mixed multitude | many who aren't of the chosen people, but go along with them
tile: The reprobate | like Pharaoh
tile: The unsaved Egyptians | who remain behind, in sin
take: It's all there.

# from 16172, 4438
--- Strong delusion
kicker: Hardened hearts
big: 2 Thessalonians 2:11-12 | mark: God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie
p: It is spiritual blindness. It is a supernatural, God-given delusion. They *cannot* receive the word of God.
p: It wasn't until I really began giving the Gospel to people, and publicly commenting on scripture, that I came to understand that when God says He blinds them who refuse to see, He means it. It's literal.

# from 9564, 13948
--- Neither will they be persuaded
kicker: Hardened hearts
scripture: Luke 16:31 | mark: neither will they be persuaded, though one rose from the dead
p: One of the most powerful means of dispensing His judgment and punishing people is God giving man what they foolishly ask for, and letting them suffer the consequences of their own decisions.
p: When someone is saved, or disobedient to death, or given up and given over to a reprobate mind, it is always with sufficient understanding of the options and tradeoffs, the truth and consequences. Free will is never exercised in ignorance. God's judgment is just, and His mercy great.
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~254 | Pharaoh as the example of how reprobation works
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~9992 | Pharaoh and the Reprobate Doctrine
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~13948 | God judges by giving men what they ask
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~16172 | God sends strong delusion

=== Knowing them by their fruits
# from 278, 6005
--- Unto every good work reprobate
kicker: Knowing them by their fruits
big: Titus 1:16 | mark: unto every good work reprobate
p: Reprobates are the children of the devil, who work all unrighteousness. Scripture teaches us to be Biblical Fundamentalists, to cling to God's word, and to reject those who seek to turn others from the truth. Their mouths must be stopped, and it is by the word of God that we shut them up.

# from 8593
--- Ye shall know them by their fruits
kicker: Knowing them by their fruits
scripture: Matthew 7:15-20 | mark: Ye shall know them by their fruits
p: They that bear thorns and briers. Thistles. Corrupt fruit. It's the same allusion, and one repeated throughout scripture. They are the tares.
refs: Hebrews 6:8; Jude 1:12; Matthew 13:24-30

# from 6899, 10711, 9467
--- A form of godliness
kicker: Knowing them by their fruits
lead: Evil, often isn't an outward appearance of malevolence like a comic book super villain. It's often someone who is a miserable human being.
p: We take pity on them often, and they use our good-natured inclination for mercy and Grace to take advantage of us. They are the false teachers, the false prophets bringing doctrines of damnation. Who have the appearance of holiness, so much so that they could fool the very elect if possible.
big: 2 Timothy 3:5-7 | mark: Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof; never able to come to the knowledge of the truth

# from 6545, 11017
--- The way of Cain
kicker: Knowing them by their fruits
scripture: Jude 1:10-13 | mark: they have gone in the way of Cain; twice dead, plucked up by the roots
p: The way of Cain is the way of works, self-righteousness, wrath, giving way to sin, and stubbornness and stiff-necked willful refusal to accept the gift of common salvation.
p: Mark them which cause divisions. Who are teaching contrary to the doctrines they have learned. We should mark them and avoid them ([[Romans 16:17-18]]).

# from 6043, 15069, 4368
--- Judge doctrine, not another's walk
kicker: Knowing them by their fruits
lead: Don't assume one's relationship with God by their works or sins. It's hypocritical and you don't know the full story, nor can you know where the Spirit may lead them.
p: But you can absolutely judge by their doctrine. And if they tell you they don't believe the Gospel and are trusting in something other than it to be justified, you can safely consider them unsaved.
big: 2 Corinthians 13:5 | mark: except ye be reprobates
p: Here is wisdom; that we can establish who is of God and who isn't by the works done. False teachers are judged by their fruit.
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6005 | Unto every good work reprobate
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~8593 | Thorns and briers rejected and burned
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6545 | The way of Cain, the first reprobate
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6043 | Judge doctrine, not another's walk

=== Past repentance
# from 8591
--- Impossible to renew them
kicker: Past repentance
scripture: Hebrews 6:4-6 | mark: it is impossible; to renew them again unto repentance
p: It's impossible for them who:
- have been enlightened to the truth; *because that which may be known of God is manifest in them*
- have tasted the gift of salvation, not accepting it but having understanding of it
- are *made partakers of the Holy Ghost,* who as Jesus said, calls all men to the truth
- *have tasted the good word of God,* they heard the word preached, they saw the revelation of God in nature, law written in their hearts

# from 8591, 8598
--- The window has closed
kicker: Past repentance
lead: It is IMPOSSIBLE for these people to be renewed again unto repentance. They can't believe. Their foolish heart was darkened. Hardened. Their conscience seared as with a hot iron.
p: Reprobation is real and it happens after God has repeatedly led one to repentance, only to be rebuffed. There is a point where it is too late, even if that point is death.
big: 1 Timothy 4:2 | mark: having their conscience seared with a hot iron

# from 10688
--- It is too late for some
kicker: Past repentance
lead: “God never gives up on us!” That's a lie. “It's never too late to repent and believe!” That's not what the Bible says.
p: As longsuffering as God is, He is clear in His word that it is too late for some.
- The people before the flood. The people of Sodom and Gomorrah.
- Pharaoh and the Egyptians. The people of Canaan who had committed abominations.
- The wicked kings and queens who killed the prophets of God.
- The Pharisees and Sadducees and scribes whom Jesus condemns in their own unbelief.
p: In the book of Daniel, Babylonian King Belshazzar saw the writing on the wall. Literally. It was too late for him.

# from 17146, 12107
--- Wisdom crieth
kicker: Past repentance
scripture: Proverbs 1:24-28 | mark: I also will laugh at your calamity; but I will not answer
p: Salvation, be it the individual soul liberty of those justified in Christ, or the physical salvation of a nation, is not extended indefinitely. God is longsuffering. He is mercy and His grace abounds. But He is clear. There comes a time for both people and nations, where His patience runs out.

# from 10688, 11392
--- The mercy of the longsuffering Lord
kicker: Past repentance
lead: It is a blessing of His mercy and grace, the longsuffering of the Lord, that for most people the final nail in their coffin is their natural passing to death and hell.
p: They have the chance to change their hearts and accept the free gift of salvation right to the end of their lives. But not all people.
big: 2 Corinthians 6:2 | mark: behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~8591 | Impossible to renew them unto repentance
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~8598 | Too late, reprobate
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~10688 | It is too late for some
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~17146 | Wisdom crieth, and God will laugh at their calamity

=== Sodom and the reprobate
# from 6993
--- Sins common to man
kicker: Sodom and the reprobate
p: We know from scripture that while man's heart is wicked, and left to our own devices, living in the flesh, all manner of natural sin afflicts us if we don't walk in the spirit, daily. Lust, envyings, lying, fearfulness, adultery, fornication, drunkenness, stealing, wrath and railing, greed and vengeance.
p: Sins all too common to man. We are all sinners, of which I am chief.
lead: But the reprobate, those who the Bible says have been rejected by God, are given over to a reprobate mind to do those things which are inconvenient. Who burn with unnatural lusts and are filled with **all unrighteousness**.

# from 6995
--- The outward sign
kicker: Sodom and the reprobate
lead: Understanding that these are rejected by God not of blood, or DNA, not by their sin, but by choice.
p: And so without excuse, they choose. And therefore, as a consequence, they are given up to vile affections. And one of the most outward signs of the reprobate mind is becoming a sodomite. Having pride in their unnatural lusts. Making their abomination their identity.
p: Now not every reprobate is a sodomite. There are some who, despite being filled with all unrighteousness, choose to not engage in sodomy. Those wolves in sheep's clothing can be recognized by other means, but some are great at hiding it.

# from 6994, 10629
--- Set forth for an example
kicker: Sodom and the reprobate
scripture: Jude 1:7 | mark: set forth for an example
p: Like the men and boys of Sodom, struck blind that the angels may protect Lot, God gives reprobates a spiritual blindness that they may not see the truth they'd so utterly rejected.
big: John 12:39-40 | mark: He hath blinded their eyes, and hardened their heart

# from 9592
--- Woe unto him through whom offences come
kicker: Sodom and the reprobate
scripture: Luke 17:1-2 | mark: woe unto him, through whom they come
p: Jesus says woe unto the person offending, the person laying snares and stumbling blocks. The person tempting another to sin. We tend to understand and focus on the direct application of this teaching, regarding those who target and corrupt children.
p: But there is a broader application to this doctrine, one few of us are willing to apply to ourselves. How often have we in our lives brought offense to another? We have a responsibility not to be a stumbling block for others. Jesus' warning is to us, too.

# from 10629
--- Pulling them from the fire
kicker: Sodom and the reprobate
lead: Sodom is a warning of their fate to those who believe not the truth when it's given.
p: It is easy in our hate of the enemies of God during their celebration of the pride, declaring their sin, to overlook the number of people in our lives and community that are on the path to perdition, for whom it isn't “too late, reprobate!” Who need the gospel.
callout: My prayer is that we can focus as much or more on giving the Gospel and being a good judge to the fatherless, the number one group headed for reprobation, that they neither are given up or perish in death, but have life everlasting in Christ Jesus. Before it is too late for them.
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6993 | The reprobate Sodomites of Genesis 19
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6995 | Sodomy as the outward sign of the reprobate mind
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~9592 | Millstone warning
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~10629 | Sodom as an example

=== Reprobate nations and leaders
# from 11633
--- Reprobate silver shall men call them
kicker: Reprobate nations and leaders
big: Jeremiah 6:30 | mark: Reprobate silver shall men call them
p: Jeremiah, in the Spirit, is preaching hard against Judah, which has become totally corrupt, and the prophets and priests are telling the people “Peace. Peace” when there is no peace. They speak soothing words, withholding judgement, leaving the people with a false sense of security.
scripture: Jeremiah 6:13-14 | mark: saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace

# from 6317
--- The wicked husbandmen
kicker: Reprobate nations and leaders
scripture: Mark 12:9 | mark: will give the vineyard unto others
p: It is amazing to us who believe that there are those who knowing the truth, seek to silence it, even with the Son of the Lord standing there in their presence.
p: It does not say He will take it from them for a time. He destroys them and gives the Kingdom to those who will produce fruit, giving God the increase, in His Son's name.

# from 950, 10892
--- Cut off for unbelief
kicker: Reprobate nations and leaders
lead: God would that they believe and be saved. But it can only happen through faith, and those who refuse to believe are cut off and made reprobate.
p: The remnant is those who believe the Gospel. Any Jew who believes will be that remnant. Same as the Greek who are grafted in to the promise by their faith.
p: A Godly nation can easily turn from the truth and be burned in the fire, just as easily as recalcitrant Israel could have a revival in Christ and be graft back in. Prodigals restored as heirs.
refs: Romans 11:5-6; Romans 11:20-23

# from 12899, 15282
--- Nations given over to idols
kicker: Reprobate nations and leaders
lead: God judges nations by their works, and especially by those who call themselves by His name. If those claiming Him fall away, He is going to cut them off.
p: The nations being driven out before Israel had fallen to Idolatry, forgotten the Lord God that brought them out of Noah and his sons. They committed abominations. Moses tells them that they will suffer the same judgment as a nation if they turn to idols.
p: The Lord says that if they don't wish to retain Him in their knowledge, they will perish for that lack of knowledge. They've been given up and given over, a reprobate nation.
refs: Deuteronomy 4:23-27; Hosea 4:6

# from 13110
--- Make no peace with reprobates
kicker: Reprobate nations and leaders
lead: There are some people who are beyond saving. There are some people whom God has given up on.
p: We are to mark and avoid, as much as possible, those we can know are reprobate. Not in wrath. Not railing. But to cut them out of our lives as much as possible, and definitely out of our congregations.
big: Romans 12:18 | mark: live peaceably with all men
p: Romans 12:18 should be our default behavior when dealing with others. But we should never declare peace with reprobates, and invite them in, lest they teach us, or our children, their abominations.
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~11633 | Reprobate silver: Judah rejected
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~6317 | The wicked husbandmen given over
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~950 | Romans 11 and the reprobate nation of Israel
read: app:doctrine-reprobate~13110 | Make no peace with reprobates

=== Why the doctrine matters
# from 2161, 10690, 13808
--- Why the doctrine matters
lead: Reprobate Doctrine is God giving you the who, the what and the why. Even the how, as far as creeping into a church unawares.
p: It explains their behavior and why their choices are made but it also gives us incentive to spread the truth and live in a way that reveals the righteousness of God, that maybe some will get it before “it's too late, reprobate!”
p: Very often Christians will be disarmed in their judgment by blindly trusting people at church. People professing to be fellow Christians. People who claim to have repented of their evil ways. It starts with denying the Reprobate Doctrine. Teaching that all men are able to be saved at any time, that it's never too late to repent.

# from 15548, 1560
--- Struggling faith versus rejecting the truth
kicker: Why the doctrine matters
lead: If a person's faith falters, fails, or is unfruitful will that person be lost? No. Of course not.
p: The difference between struggling with faith and having doubt after being saved vs rejection of the truth they understood but never trusted in, to believe a lie. Don't be confused.
big: John 6:64 | mark: Jesus knew from the beginning who they were that believed not
read: believers-cannot-apostatize | Believers Cannot Apostatize
read: topic-assurance-eternal-security | Eternal Security

# from 8758
--- Not by our bad report
kicker: Why the doctrine matters
lead: This isn't simply for the cursing of those who have been rejected by way of their hardened heart, but a grave warning to those of us who have been blessed by the faith in God's promise and redeemed in the blood of Christ.
p: Faith comes by hearing the word of God. So does reprobation.
p: Rather, if they reject the truth of God and His offer of grace and mercy, let it be because of our righteous conversation. Our behavior. That they see our faith and that we walk the straight paths.
take: This is a great responsibility.

# from 15287, 15288, 8598, 12074
--- Before it is too late [title]
overline: The reprobate mind
heading: Seek the Lord while He may be found
center: God's offer of salvation is not available to all men forever. There comes a time when it is too late, reprobate! So don't delay, don't put it off. Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ and be saved.
big: Isaiah 55:6-7 | mark: Seek ye the LORD while he may be found

--- Before it is too late, continued
center: If you do not know for sure, today, right now, that you are saved, please consider His word. Don't wait. Now is the time. Accept that free gift.
refs: Acts 16:31; Romans 10:13; Hebrews 3:15
note: Every teaching is on the [[app:doctrine-reprobate|The reprobate mind]] page.
